---
export const prerender = false

import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { getSite } from '../lib/config'
import { safeExternalUrl } from '../lib/security'
import { WEBHOOK_BIN_TTL_MS } from '../lib/webhook-store'

// One page for the whole site: the terms are the same for every tool and game,
// and one text cannot drift from a second copy of itself. Every number below is
// read from the module that enforces it, so the page cannot promise a shorter
// retention than the code keeps. noindex: it is linked from every footer, and a
// legal page in search results helps no one find a tool.
const site = await getSite(Astro.locals)
const github = safeExternalUrl(site.social.github)
const binHours = Math.round(WEBHOOK_BIN_TTL_MS / 3_600_000)
const LAST_UPDATED = '25 October 2026'
const BOARD_DAYS = 7
const ANALYTICS_DAYS = 90
---

<Base
  title="terms & privacy"
  description="The terms for using the tools and games on this site, and exactly what each one keeps."
  noindex
>
  <article data-type="terms">
    <h1>Terms &amp; privacy</h1>
    <p data-type="terms-updated">Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>

    <h2>Using the site</h2>
    <p>
      Everything here is free to use, for anything, with no account. The tools
      and games are offered as-is, without any warranty: they may be wrong,
      slow or unavailable, and they can change or go away at any time. Check
      anything important before you rely on it. To the extent the law
      allows, {site.name} is not liable for any loss that comes from using the site.
    </p>
    <p>
      Please don't use the server tools to attack, flood or probe systems you
      have no permission to test. They are rate-limited, and abusive traffic is
      blocked.
    </p>

    <h2>What stays in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      Most tools run entirely on your device. Your inputs, settings and last
      results may be saved in your browser's local storage so they are still
      there next time; that storage never leaves your device, and clearing your
      browser data removes it. The site itself sets no cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>What the server tools see</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Webhook Inspector</strong> stores the requests sent to your
        capture URL (method, headers, body, and the sender's IP address) in
        the server's memory, so you can read them. Anyone who has the URL can
        see them. A capture URL and its requests are deleted after {binHours} hours
        without activity, and on every server restart. Don't send real
        passwords or production secrets to it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Link Peek</strong> fetches the public URL you enter, and the
        image it names, to show how it unfurls. Nothing about the page or your
        request is kept.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Chainsaw</strong> opens a TLS connection to the host you enter
        and reads its certificates. Nothing is kept. A shared result link
        carries the host name in the URL.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>DNS Sightline</strong> sends your domain's DNS questions to
        three public resolvers (Cloudflare, Google and Quad9). Nothing is kept.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To keep these tools available, the server counts recent requests per
      address for rate limiting. Those counts live in memory for a short time
      and are never written to disk.
    </p>

    <h2>Leaderboards</h2>
    <p>
      The Type Trial and Hue Hunt daily boards store the name you type and your
      score for that day, and show them publicly. Boards are deleted
      after {BOARD_DAYS} days. Use a nickname if you prefer.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The site keeps aggregate counts only: how many times each page was served
      per day, the visitor's country, the website that linked to it (the host
      name, never the full address), and page-speed measurements. It keeps no IP
      addresses, no user agents and no visitor or session identifiers, so none
      of it can be traced back to you. Counts are kept
      for {ANALYTICS_DAYS} days.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may change; the date at the top says when they last did.{' '}
      {github
        ? <>Questions or a problem to report? Reach {site.name} on <a href={github} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.</>
        : <>Questions or a problem to report? Use the links in the footer.</>}
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  article[data-type="terms"] {
    max-width: 42rem;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-section);
  }

  p[data-type="terms-updated"] {
    margin-top: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  article[data-type="terms"] h2 {
    margin: var(--space-section) 0 var(--space-xs);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }

  article[data-type="terms"] p,
  article[data-type="terms"] li {
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  article[data-type="terms"] ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-card);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }
</style>
